# .env.op — 1Password reference manifest. GIT-TRACKED. op:// references ONLY, never values.
#
# Each line maps an env-var name to its 1Password location:
#   VAR_NAME=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# The VAR names here are exactly what the ${env:VAR} (.cursor/mcp.json) / ${VAR:-} (root .mcp.json)
# placeholders resolve to at runtime. Placeholders never change — only delivery does (INVARIANT 2).
#
# Delivered per surface, OUTSIDE this repo (you never invoke it):
#   local        chezmoi -> launchctl cache (biometric `op`)
#   Claude cloud SessionStart .claude/hooks/bootstrap-secrets.sh (op inject -> $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE)
#   GitHub CI    op inject via sa-ci (1Password CLI)
#
# Requires `!.env.op` in .gitignore so this file travels to cloud/CI. Safe to commit (op:// refs are
# structural metadata, not secrets). NEVER commit a resolved value or an `ops_` Service-Account token.
#
# Add one line per secret this repo needs, e.g.:
#   EXAMPLE_API_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
